cope (table desc) | subject per term, registrar rollup (concept comparison) | subject/cluster per term, final registrar enrollment (concept comparison) |\n| Coverage | \"may not cover all subjects\" — program snapshot (column_concept comparison) | full registrar offerings | full registrar offerings |\n| Degree-granting dept join | OFFER_DEPT_CODE → SIS_DEPARTMENT (documented) | OFFER_DEPT_CODE → SIS_DEPARTMENT | DEPARTMENT_CODE → SIS_DEPARTMENT |\n| Precedents for this task shape | dw_1165, dw_1350 (VARIANCE/AVG of TIP NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per degree-granting dept) | dw_1212 (units stats), dw_4527 | dw_4812, dw_4683 |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n- Required measure \"number of enrolled students\": SUPPORTED by TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (hint explicitly maps it); also supported by other tables but not hinted.\n- \"subjects offered by that department\" via OFFER_DEPT_CODE↔DEPARTMENT_CODE: SUPPORTED (hint join key; documented in column desc).\n- \"departments that grant degrees\": only SIS_DEPARTMENT carries IS_DEGREE_GRANTING (concept_department_dimension comparison: STUDENT_DEPARTMENT has \"no degree-granting flag\") → SIS_DEPARTMENT SUPPORTED, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT NOT-SUPPORTED.\n- \"students in their fourth year\": only MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries STUDENT_YEAR → SUPPORTED.\n- \"Mathematics department\": SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' (hint; dw_1212 precedent) → SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"students in their fourth year\" → MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR (hint mapping). Precedent dw_1212/dw_2759 use `STUDENT_YEAR = 'G'` for graduate; by the same coding convention, fourth-year undergraduates are `STUDENT_YEAR = '4'`. I could not verify the value domain via mysql_query (DB access denied) — this is the one unverified literal.\n- \"departments that grant degrees\" → `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'` (dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_1212 all use `= 'Y'`).\n- \"Mathematics department\" → `DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'` (dw_1212 precedent).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- \"variance/avg/stddev of NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per degree-granting department\" precedents on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: 2 (dw_1165 — VARIANCE; dw_1350 — AVG/VARIANCE). Both join SIS_DEPARTMENT on OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'.\n- Same-shape statistics on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_SUMMARY exist (dw_4527, dw_2958) but the task hint names TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: consumed by textbook-material metrics (dw_1165, dw_2591, dw_3398) and department enrollment-dispersion statistics (dw_1165, dw_1350); parent of TIP_DETAIL.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: the canonical department dimension for degree-granting and school filters (concept decision_guide: \"Questions filtering departments by school or degree-granting status → Use SIS_DEPARTMENT\").\n- **MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY**: used for per-department student counts/filters (dw_1350 Peter-students, dw_1212 graduate counts, dw_2759, dw_100).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓ (columns), graph evidence via metric SQL ✓\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓\n- column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_department_name — semantic_get / search ✓\n- concept_department_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_person_directory, concept_course_material_programs — semantic_get / search ✓\n- Metrics dw_1165, dw_1350, dw_1212 — semantic_get with full SQL ✓; dw_2958, dw_3356, dw_4527, dw_4640, dw_1033, dw_100, dw_2759, dw_2240, dw_1474, dw_3237 — descriptions reviewed via search ✓\n- mysql_query attempted 4 times — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" (database unavailable for verification; noted explicitly).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (measure), joined TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; filters SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y', SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'; join SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT with MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR = '4'; GROUP BY SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Single-level aggregation per department (only Mathematics survives the filter, so one output row). Use bare `AVG()`, `VARIANCE()`, `STDDEV()` — no rounding. The student join fans out subject rows by the number of fourth-year Mathematics students, but since every subject row is replicated the same constant number of times within the single department group, AVG/VARIANCE/STDDEV values are mathematically unchanged; this matches the hint's prescribed three-table join.\n\n**6c. Reasons:**\n- *Data*: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is subject-per-term grain with NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS present; SIS_DEPARTMENT is one row per department (no fan-out on that join); only MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY has STUDENT_YEAR.\n- *Semantic-network*: hint join keys match documented column descs; concept_department_dimension decision_guide mandates SIS_DEPARTMENT for degree-granting filters.\n- *Business*: dw_1165 and dw_1350 are exact precedents for \"variance/avg of TIP enrolled students per degree-granting department\"; dw_1212 is the precedent for combining Mathematics-department subject stats with a student-directory year filter.\n\n**6d. Caveat:** The literal `'4'` for fourth-year students could not be data-verified due to the database access failure; it follows the STUDENT_YEAR coding convention evidenced by `STUDENT_YEAR = 'G'` (graduate) in dw_1212/dw_2759.\n\n",
